# router_yilin — Router container usage notes
# Image: yilin-router (P1/docker-images/router/Dockerfile)
# Adapters: 2 (eth0 for underlay, eth1 for host-facing) — adjust as needed
# Console: telnet (open from GNS3)
# Important: The image must not set any default IP addresses. Configure IPs per-topology.
# FRR services enabled in image: zebra, bgpd, ospfd, isisd
# Example runtime steps after starting node in GNS3:
#
#   # verify interfaces
#   ip addr
#   # assign IP to underlay interface
#   ip addr add 192.0.2.2/24 dev eth0
#   ip link set eth0 up
#   # assign IP to host-facing interface (if needed)
#   ip addr add 10.0.0.1/24 dev eth1
#   ip link set eth1 up
#   # ensure kernel forwarding is enabled (image sets sysctl, but verify):
#   sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward
#   # check FRR daemons
#   ps -ef | grep -E 'zebra|bgpd|ospfd|isisd|frr'
#   vtysh -c "show running-config"
#
# Router node naming convention: use your login in the node name.
# Example: `router_yilin` (where `yilin` is your login).
